.TH SETITIMER 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
setitimer \- set an interval timer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/time.h>
.B int setitimer(int which, const struct itimerval* value, struct itimerval* previous);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sets ITIMER_REAL, ITIMER_VIRTUAL or ITIMER_PROF. A zero it_value disarms the
timer; a nonzero it_interval enables periodic delivery. If previous is not
NULL, it receives the prior timer state. Linux also permits a NULL value,
with Linux\-specific behavior; portable callers should supply a value.
ITIMER_REAL and alarm share a timer.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getitimer (3crunch),
.BR alarm (3crunch),
.BR setitimer (2)
